WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.770
Seeing what is going on
in our country,

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:06.973
I'm not going to have
a normal show tonight.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:09.475
I'm going to have
a different kind of show.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.445
I'm going to start this
personally and then expand out

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:15.315
because that's where
we all need to start --

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:19.085
with ourselves and looking
at ourselves in the mirror.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.487
And I had to
really examine myself --

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:23.589
really examine myself
in the mirror this week

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:26.659
because a story came out
about me on "SNL"

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.729
doing an impression
of Chris Rock in blackface.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.198
And I was horrified.

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.432
Not of the fact that people

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:36.001
were trying to cancel me
or cancel the show,

00:00:36.001 --> 00:00:37.704
which is scary enough.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.939
But the thing
that haunts me the most was,

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:43.976
How do I say,
"I love this person?

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:48.114
I respect this guy more
than I respect most humans.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:52.385
I'm not a racist.
I don't feel this way."

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:55.721
And instead,
what I kept getting advised was

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.924
to just stay quiet
and to not say anything,

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:01.528
and that's the advice,
because we're all afraid.

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:03.362
And I took it for a minute.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.464
I took the advice,
and thought,

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.133
"God, I'm going to do this
wrong. You're right.

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.501
I'm going to say something

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.402
and get myself
into even more trouble.

00:01:10.402 --> 00:01:14.673
I'm going to make this worse.
I don't know what to do."

00:01:14.673 --> 00:01:16.842
So I thought about it,

00:01:16.842 --> 00:01:21.380
and I realized that
I can't not say I'm horrified

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.884
and I'm sorry
and I'm embarrassed.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:30.489
And what that small gesture did
for me was break my own silence.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:33.492
And what then I started to do
was talk to some experts,

00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.561
some of which are here
tonight and this week,

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:39.399
and I realized that the silence
is the biggest crime

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.134
that white guys like me
and the rest of us are doing.

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:43.802
Staying silent.

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:45.371
We need to say something.

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.273
We need to keep
saying something.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.608
And we need to stop saying,
"That's not okay,"

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:52.411
more than just one day
on Twitter.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.714
I realize I needed
to get educated

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.248
about how to stop the silence

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:58.384
and the fear
of saying the wrong thing

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:02.288
by not being silent and
stepping out and stepping up.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:07.193
But I need to be -- We all need
to be talking about this.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.261
And I spoke to someone
incredible and brilliant

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:11.865
who I think can help us all out
a little bit here

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.566
in this incredibly sensitive

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:16.302
and in-our-face subject
that we need to deal with.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:18.404
We cannot try
to bury this again.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.374
It's not going to get buried.
It's not going away.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.809
We can't just hope that
everyone loves each other.

00:02:23.809 --> 00:02:26.845
We can't say, "Be the change,"
and just sit around tweeting,

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:29.315
"Be the change, be the change."

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.750
What is the change?
How do I change?

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.921
How do I do it? What do I do?
Can I wear a T-shirt?

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.590
Is there a color?
Is there a sign?

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.025
Is there a way to do this?
I don't know.

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:42.061
So let's start talking
with some people about this

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.764
and try to get proactive
and activated

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:48.701
in this love,
in this change cycle.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.969
So let's figure out

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.504
how we're going to
get along with each other.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.440
Let's figure out how we're going
to stop this senseless violence

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:56.009
that erupts and disrupts

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.912
the entire country
and now the world.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:01.847
The world is screaming,
and it is angry,

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:04.517
and we all need to figure out
a way to take the anger,

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.720
which, of course,
is just sadness and fear,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.123
and do something with it and
try to actually dig this up.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:13.693
This is such a long root
in the ground.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.995
It is so long and deep,

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:19.232
but we got to get in there,
and we have to dig it up.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:22.935
I don't know how else to do it.
I'm clearly not an expert.

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.871
I'm clearly
a late-night talk show host,

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.872
and I screwed it up already.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:34.213
So let's go. Let's reform.
Let's talk. Let's do it.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.716
My first guest tonight
is Derrick Johnson,

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.752
the president and CEO
of the NAACP.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:43.523
We're going to open the show
with him tonight and just talk.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:46.125
Here we go.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.526
Derrick, thank you so much

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:49.162
for being a guest
on our show tonight.

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:51.630
I know you must be very, very
busy, so I appreciate this.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.033
-Well, it's a pleasure
to be here,

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:58.371
and I do want to respond
to your opening monologue.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:59.939
That was powerful,

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.641
but most importantly
that's about courage.

00:04:02.641 --> 00:04:07.079
In this time of many people
searching for answers

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:12.885
and just the display of anger
and hopelessness and wandering,

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:15.187
more people need to speak about

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:18.224
where they are
with a really authentic voice.

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:20.126
And I think you did that
with the opening monologue,

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:23.229
so thank you for those words.

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:25.298
-With all the things
that are happening right now,

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:27.800
I mean,
there's so much to talk about.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:33.205
But I personally want to know
how I can do better

00:04:33.205 --> 00:04:36.375
and take responsibility
for how I act

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.945
both consciously
and unconsciously.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:42.881
And so we talked about this --
I talked to you --

00:04:42.881 --> 00:04:44.216
thank you very much --

00:04:44.216 --> 00:04:46.452
about my mistakes
I made in the past,

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:51.056
and I want to move forward,
going forward.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:53.726
I want to work on
being a better ally.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:58.764
-You know,
we are all born flawed,

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:02.268
but flawed is part of
the journey that we are on

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:05.304
so we can try
to get to perfection.

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:09.008
And if anyone can stand up and
say, "I haven't made a mistake,"

00:05:09.008 --> 00:05:12.044
run, because that person
is clearly a liar.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.580
We have an opportunity
to move forward.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.983
We have an opportunity
to open up dialogue.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:20.219
We have an opportunity to learn
to understand one another.

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:24.256
-How do we keep
the momentum going?

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:26.558
-You know,
one of the worst things

00:05:26.558 --> 00:05:29.728
about these moments
of realization

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:31.463
is people want to have

00:05:31.463 --> 00:05:35.467
a quick-fix outpour and then
go back to their corners.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:38.370
The way we keep
the momentum going

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.973
is keeping the dialogue open,

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:45.110
appreciating the uniqueness
we all bring to the table,

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.113
and celebrating that uniqueness

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:51.016
and not allowing demagogues
to create otherness

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:53.453
from people
who may be different.

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:56.255
-I know that I'm getting
a lot of advice from you,

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:59.891
but, also,
I think it's important to know

00:05:59.891 --> 00:06:02.728
that white people should be
talking to white people

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:05.898
about racism, as well.
-Yeah.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:08.133
-Can you talk about that
a little?

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:12.838
-So, racism is
a learned behavior.

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:17.643
And for us to unlearn behavior,
we have to be honest about it

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:19.845
and create spaces
where we can talk about it.

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:21.180
And I appreciate you.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.017
But most importantly
be the example we want to see.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:27.854
And so peer-to-peer
conversations,

00:06:27.854 --> 00:06:32.892
using one's platform to promote
a more positive outlook at life

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:36.529
as it relates to other people's
uniqueness and difference

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.531
becomes important.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:41.067
You know, you and I,
we've talked about

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:44.136
building out a campaign
looking forward.

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:48.708
And once we launch it,
I hope others will join in.

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:51.643
The beautiful thing
about where we are today --

00:06:51.643 --> 00:06:56.515
media is so democratized
that anyone of us can be

00:06:56.515 --> 00:07:00.185
our own news channel,
our own information source.

00:07:00.185 --> 00:07:03.322
And for celebrity types
with huge following

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:05.992
on their social-media platforms,

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:08.927
it's really important
that we start amplifying

00:07:08.927 --> 00:07:11.163
lines of communication

00:07:11.163 --> 00:07:14.967
that opens up the issue
of being anti-racist,

00:07:14.967 --> 00:07:18.938
to talk about the uniqueness
of who we are as Americans,

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:22.074
and to really promote
a more positive dialogue

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.177
with one another to do better

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:28.547
and then not allow demagogues
sitting in particular seats

00:07:28.547 --> 00:07:32.384
to drive a wedge
between communities.

00:07:32.384 --> 00:07:36.221
-I've heard that term
"anti-racist" now.

00:07:36.221 --> 00:07:38.524
It's, like, kind of a buzzword
now on Twitter.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:39.925
What does it actually --

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:41.927
What does it mean? Anti-racist?

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:45.164
-It means that you're actually
fighting against racism,

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:48.734
that you are consciously
doing things

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.903
to stop the spread of racism.

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:53.606
We also understand
that racism is structural,

00:07:53.606 --> 00:07:55.641
it's institutionalized,

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:57.643
and that as much as you benefit

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:59.812
from that structure
and that institution,

00:07:59.812 --> 00:08:02.214
you fight to remove
that structure

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:03.615
and those institutions

00:08:03.615 --> 00:08:06.552
so others can have
a level playing field.

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:09.188
We have not had a level
playing field in this country

00:08:09.188 --> 00:08:12.758
since its inception,
and we need to create a way

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.326
that we can all be celebrated

00:08:14.326 --> 00:08:16.962
and all the excellence
that we bring to the table

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:21.033
can be appreciated by the
communities across the country.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:24.035
Think about where we would have
been without a Motown,

00:08:24.035 --> 00:08:25.470
with all that creativity.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:28.541
Can you imagine
what it would feel like

00:08:28.541 --> 00:08:31.310
if you never heard the voice
of Aretha Franklin?

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:34.546
Think about that fact
that you have the comedic genius

00:08:34.546 --> 00:08:37.783
of Eddie Murphy or Chris Rock,
one of your friends.

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:40.219
That's what this is about.

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:42.154
How do you remove those barriers

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.555
so we can have
more Aretha Franklins,

00:08:43.555 --> 00:08:44.923
we can have more Eddie Murphys,

00:08:44.923 --> 00:08:48.294
we can all get down
with Beyoncé and Jay-Z?

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:50.229
That's what we're talking about,

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:52.631
because there's so much
we are losing

00:08:52.631 --> 00:08:54.834
as a result
of the structural barriers

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:58.170
and institutional racism
that currently exists.

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:01.506
-This moment happening now,

00:09:01.506 --> 00:09:05.177
would you compare it to any
other moment in our history?

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:06.646
-You know, it's fascinating.

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:11.050
I just spoke earlier
about the last 70 days

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.620
is perhaps the worst
in our history in my opinion

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.388
since the Civil War.

00:09:16.388 --> 00:09:22.161
We opened up the last 70 days
with a global pandemic

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:25.330
and an anemic response
from the federal government

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:31.971
causing mass spread of a virus
gone unaddressed too long.

00:09:31.971 --> 00:09:34.339
Then we realize,
for the African-Americans,

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:36.242
that we were being
disproportionately impacted,

00:09:36.242 --> 00:09:38.343
we didn't have enough tests,

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:42.981
only to fall into our normal
state of aggressive policing

00:09:42.981 --> 00:09:45.551
in our communities,
first in Georgia.

00:09:45.551 --> 00:09:48.020
Then to learn that someone
was killed in her bed

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.822
in Louisville, Kentucky,

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:52.324
followed by the incident
in Minneapolis,

00:09:52.324 --> 00:09:54.893
followed by the woman
in Central Park.

00:09:54.893 --> 00:09:59.365
Only for people to stand up
to have peaceful protests

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:00.699
because the district attorney

00:10:00.699 --> 00:10:03.802
refused to bring those officers
to justice,

00:10:03.802 --> 00:10:07.439
moving that along to violence
in the street

00:10:07.439 --> 00:10:10.609
all under the backdrop
of economic collapse.

00:10:10.609 --> 00:10:13.179
We have had a rough 70 days,

00:10:13.179 --> 00:10:16.915
and we must stand up
against what's taking place.

00:10:16.915 --> 00:10:20.786
-And we can take this,
hopefully, this moment

00:10:20.786 --> 00:10:24.289
and turn it
into something positive.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:25.725
-We can.
I mean, it starts today.

00:10:25.725 --> 00:10:28.059
It starts with us
having this dialogue.

00:10:28.059 --> 00:10:30.195
It starts with us understanding

00:10:30.195 --> 00:10:33.265
that we need to drive people
to do something.

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:37.303
For us, you know, you go
on our website, NAACP.org,

00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:40.773
and join us as volunteers,
join the organization

00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:44.743
because we have to address
the structural racism,

00:10:44.743 --> 00:10:47.413
the systemic issues
that's plagued this country

00:10:47.413 --> 00:10:50.349
for far too long,
and we must do it together.

00:10:50.349 --> 00:10:53.285
It's not just the burden
of African-Americans.

00:10:53.285 --> 00:10:56.789
It's the burden of all Americans
and whites to join in.

00:10:56.789 --> 00:11:01.193
This is an opportunity for us to
do better so we can be better.

00:11:01.193 --> 00:11:04.063
-We should have
everyone watching --

00:11:04.063 --> 00:11:08.300
I'd love them to go to NAACP.org
and do what you can,

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:11.203
register in there
and donate and help.

00:11:11.203 --> 00:11:13.972
-Navigate the website.
We're going to talk about --

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:16.308
If you want to just donate
and stuff, great.

00:11:16.308 --> 00:11:19.444
If you want to join,
we want you to join.

00:11:19.444 --> 00:11:22.114
NAACP, we are all races.

00:11:22.114 --> 00:11:24.950
Our founding was both
black, white, male, female.

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.819
We don't discriminate.
We have LGBT.

00:11:27.819 --> 00:11:30.655
We don't discriminate
because we believe everyone

00:11:30.655 --> 00:11:32.424
should be afforded
equal protection

00:11:32.424 --> 00:11:34.526
under the law, so therefore
we operate that way.

00:11:34.526 --> 00:11:37.329
If you want to get engaged
and be a volunteer,

00:11:37.329 --> 00:11:39.498
it's all there -- NAACP.org.

00:11:39.498 --> 00:11:40.933
We need your support

00:11:40.933 --> 00:11:43.935
so we can make democracy
work for everyone.

00:11:43.935 --> 00:11:47.772
-I want to work with you,
Derrick, and the NAACP,

00:11:47.772 --> 00:11:51.143
so if you don't mind,
I'd like to check in with you

00:11:51.143 --> 00:11:53.913
every couple of months
just to see how I'm doing

00:11:53.913 --> 00:11:56.015
and what else
I could be doing to help.

00:11:56.015 --> 00:11:57.783
Is that okay?
-I'm looking forward to it.

00:11:57.783 --> 00:11:59.818
And, Jimmy, historical note.

00:11:59.818 --> 00:12:04.489
The Civil Rights Movement was
anchored by some entertainers.

00:12:04.489 --> 00:12:07.726
And it was Harry Belafonte.
It was Sidney Poitier.

00:12:07.726 --> 00:12:09.495
And it was Dick Gregory.

00:12:09.495 --> 00:12:11.163
And they reached
across the aisle,

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:12.998
and they went and got Bob Dylan,

00:12:12.998 --> 00:12:14.867
and they went
and got Marlon Brando

00:12:14.867 --> 00:12:18.336
and many others to make sure
that it was the type

00:12:18.336 --> 00:12:22.274
of support necessary
to move an agenda

00:12:22.274 --> 00:12:24.642
that everyone
could benefit from.

00:12:24.642 --> 00:12:29.147
To be anti-racist, it means
joining in on this army

00:12:29.147 --> 00:12:31.317
to fight against racism.

00:12:31.317 --> 00:12:34.587
So join the NAACP so we can
fight against racism together.

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:36.955
-Derrick,
thank you so much again.

00:12:36.955 --> 00:12:40.760
I appreciate this.
-Thank you for the opportunity.

